t''s agents, and the tab icons, needs-you flag and move locks keep reading Snapshot.Agents (M.ORCH-T837); d5485d83 Ctrl+Left/Ctrl+Right switch CLI tabs even while a terminal has focus (M.ORCH-T824); db037d27 Halve the 5-hour utilization chart height from 260 to 130 (M.ORCH-T877); 1b2a30a2 Remove the person toolbar''s clock, refresh info, Refresh button and Open Launcher rocket, with the Clock view model, RefreshInfo and OpenLauncherCommand only they used; a closed Launcher tab reopens on the next refresh and a stale refresh failure clears (M.ORCH-T855); 99bbe28e Stop raising the pacing toasts (Pacing, Coasting, At the limit): the 5-hour chart and its caption already say it (M.ORCH-T857); b7d48817 Standardize padding, margins and gutters on one 4/8/12/16/24 spacing scale defined in App.xaml (M.ORCH-T853); 4e940cf1 Fix LimitWakerTests weekday test to assert the nudge-era wording ''stopped for the limit at <weekday time>'' (M.ORCH-T876))', '32b8385d', 894, NULL);
INSERT INTO tickets (id, repo, number, date, type, status, summary, ref, ordinal, row_md) VALUES ('M.ORCH-T896', 'MindAttic.Orchestrator', 896, '2026-10-25', 'fix', 'closed', 'orchestrator next --claim prompt: ''Then run /commit, but don''t push (the next step does)'' makes Sonnet subagents stop after committing and report ''not pushed, as instructed'' (U.CHN-T62, U.RICO-T37, U.RICO-T20 on 2026-10-25 each needed a nudge to review, rebase, push and close); reword so the commit step is clearly one step of several, e.g. ''commit with /commit (no push yet), then continue:'' and end with ''you are done only when the ticket is closed''', '0233fe77', 895, NULL);
INSERT INTO tickets (id, repo, number, date, type, status, summary, ref, ordinal, row_md) VALUES ('M.ORCH-T897', 'MindAttic.Orchestrator', 897, '2026-10-25', 'fix', 'closed', 'Fails on main: MindAttic.Orchestrator.Tests.TabStatusTests.The_strip_shows_the_light_and_week_left_and_the_API_key_switch_lives_on_its_tab — Assert.That(strip, Does.Contain("x:Name=\"TabBusyIcon\"").And.Contain("Loaded=\"TabBusyIcon_Loaded\"").And.Contain("IsVisibleChanged=\"TabBusyIcon_IsVisibleChanged\"")) Expected: String containing "x:Name="TabBusyIcon"" and String containing "Loaded="TabBusyIcon_Loaded"" and containing "IsVisible... (landed on main since the last green run: tickets M.ORCH-T879, M.ORCH-T890, M.ORCH-T872, M.ORCH-T849, M.ORCH-T887, M.ORCH-T878, M.ORCH-T863, M.ORCH-T886, M.ORCH-T885, M.ORCH-T866, M.ORCH-T867, M.ORCH-T884, M.ORCH-T862, M.ORCH-T846, M.ORCH-T842 in e4852036 Subscribe the dashboard to the app bus: ticket ids open in a listening Tickets Desktop over the bus, Tickets Desktop''s "show who is working X" selects that person and CLI tab, and ticket events refresh the Queue instead of a poll (M.ORCH-T879); 94705792 Carry ticket events on the status bus: the daemon publishes every ticket change from the ticket database''s change feed, and the Orchestrator publishes its own claims and releases as it makes them (M.ORCH-T879); bc6d311f Flash the person tab''s status icon as a pause once every open CLI of that login is idle (no turn, subagent, claim or prompt, judged as orchestrator busy does), steady green play while any works, steady pause with none open; opacity pulse honours reduced motion, word kept in tooltip and accessible name (M.ORCH-T890); a395638b Lay pushed snapshot figures straight onto the dashboard and drop its stream-up poll to a 5-minute heartbeat (M.ORCH-T872); b33ddd15 Give the daemon a status inbox the hooks write to directly, instead of it noticing their files (M.ORCH-T872); 9c54d60e Carry each snapshot''s own figures on the status stream in an extensible kind/version/payload envelope (M.ORCH-T872); 11ddc58a Expect the Queue status strip in the tab-strip test: QueueStatusTabs (M.ORCH-T849) is a bare library MaTabControl with no colour of its own (M.ORCH-T887); 2aceb918 Add a Tickets button beside the dashboard''s settings cog: Segoe''s Tag glyph (E8EC) in MaToolButton style, "Open Tickets" tooltip and automation name; it brings a running Tickets Desktop''s window forward (by process main window handle, TerminalFocus.Foreground) or starts the installed exe (C:\Apps or %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs, where MindAttic.Tickets/deploy.ps1 puts it), and toasts when it isn''t installed; all exceptions contained (M.ORCH-T878); 000dd0e8 Order the queue newest-created first with each ticket''s open prerequisites pulled ahead of it, transitively: an explicit priority (tickets ticket bump/priority, the daemon''s failing-test fixes) still outranks recency; same date, the higher ticket number is newer; cycles are broken safely; a blocked ticket is still never proposed or handed out before its prerequisite closes; orchestrator queue explains the order and marks prerequisites "required by"; NUnit tests for the ordering and existing tests updated to it (M.ORCH-T863); 9bca3c3a Fix DeployScriptTests: assert --force is added to the installer args under -Force, not one exact array literal (M.ORCH-T886); bd2c14b8 Move the spacing tokens out of App.xaml into Themes/Spacing.xaml so App.xaml keeps no resource of its own but Visible, and pin that the dictionary holds only Thickness and double tokens (M.ORCH-T885); fe308a5f Ctrl+X in an embedded terminal cuts its selected text: a terminal''s screen text can''t be removed, so the selection is copied to the clipboard and cleared; with no selection (or one that can''t be read) Ctrl+X goes to the CLI unchanged. Plain Ctrl+X only; NUnit tests for the cut chord (M.ORCH-T866); 51bb8fb5 Ctrl+C in an embedded terminal copies its selected text to the clipboard: taken before the native terminal sees it only when TerminalControl.GetSelectedText returns a selection (which it clears); with none, or one that can''t be read, the key still reaches the CLI as its ^C interrupt. Plain Ctrl+C only, every fault contained, the held chord''s repeats after a copy swallowed; NUnit tests for the chord and the take logic (M.ORCH-T867); 406766e6 Read a subagent''s ticket from prompts like ''Work on ticket X (feature, approved)'': the type had to be one bare word, so feature and chore subagents were never seen working their tickets and their claims counted as pending for hours (M.ORCH-T884); 2397a5e0 Add NUnit tests for the session-restore file: save and load, rotation keeping the last runs and never deleting on read, an unreadable file, when to offer, and each tab''s reopen request (resume, fresh, stale resume replaced, Launcher menu, other providers, a CLI moved to another login) (M.ORCH-T862); d71ade23 Write the dashboard''s session-restore file continuously and offer it back after a crash: rewritten whenever a terminal tab opens, closes or moves, a session is learned or the selection changes; a last write from the crash handlers and ProcessExit; marked clean on a clean exit (an upgrade or Windows logoff isn''t); the next start offers to reopen an unclean run''s tabs, each Claude CLI resuming its session on its login, then reselects the person and tab (M.ORCH-T862); b3b1dfe9 Add the session-restore file''s model and store, and learn each terminal tab''s Claude session: RestoreState/RestoreTab, SessionRestoreStore (atomic temp-then-move writes, rotation keeping the last 5 runs'' files, ReopenRequest building a tab''s claude --resume reopen from its PaneRequest), and TerminalsViewModel.Update matching each pane''s Launcher host or process tree to the session-context pid''s session (M.ORCH-T862); c842f705 Add Active / Pending / Closed / Won''t do tabs to each person''s Queue on the dashboard, each with its count and Active first: Active is their open tickets claimed or being worked, Pending the open ones waiting (unapproved, on a prerequisite, or queued), Closed and Won''t do the ones closed in the last 7 days, read off the UI thread from the ticket database by ClosedTicketSource (at most once a minute, each ticket''s history once, bounded per read). ReloadTicketQueues is the one load a pushed ticket event can call later; every failure is contained (M.ORCH-T849); c8e059da Keep keystrokes and focus on the embedded CLI: while a terminal holds focus only F5, Ctrl+Tab/Ctrl+Shift+Tab, Ctrl+Left/Right and the paste keys stay the dashboard''s; every other window KeyBinding (Esc, the zoom keys Ctrl+Plus/Minus/0) is gated so its key reaches the CLI, and focus returns to the shown CLI''s terminal after window activation, a person-tab switch, a dialog closing, a toast, a page click or a refresh that dropped the focused element, unless a text box, menu or dialog holds it (M.ORCH-T846); 2bd539e4 Show only a person''s own assigned queue on their page: the Unassigned tickets heading and list now show on the global login''s tab alone (ShowsUnassignedTickets), the dashboard''s one place to see an unassigned ticket and reach Assign in Tickets, and only that tab fills UnassignedTickets (M.ORCH-T842))', '4980d446', 896, NULL);
