oard and cleared; with no selection (or one that can''t be read) Ctrl+X goes to the CLI unchanged. Plain Ctrl+X only; NUnit tests for the cut chord (M.ORCH-T866); 51bb8fb5 Ctrl+C in an embedded terminal copies its selected text to the clipboard: taken before the native terminal sees it only when TerminalControl.GetSelectedText returns a selection (which it clears); with none, or one that can''t be read, the key still reaches the CLI as its ^C interrupt. Plain Ctrl+C only, every fault contained, the held chord''s repeats after a copy swallowed; NUnit tests for the chord and the take logic (M.ORCH-T867); 406766e6 Read a subagent''s ticket from prompts like ''Work on ticket X (feature, approved)'': the type had to be one bare word, so feature and chore subagents were never seen working their tickets and their claims counted as pending for hours (M.ORCH-T884); 2397a5e0 Add NUnit tests for the session-restore file: save and load, rotation keeping the last runs and never deleting on read, an unreadable file, when to offer, and each tab''s reopen request (resume, fresh, stale resume replaced, Launcher menu, other providers, a CLI moved to another login) (M.ORCH-T862); d71ade23 Write the dashboard''s session-restore file continuously and offer it back after a crash: rewritten whenever a terminal tab opens, closes or moves, a session is learned or the selection changes; a last write from the crash handlers and ProcessExit; marked clean on a clean exit (an upgrade or Windows logoff isn''t); the next start offers to reopen an unclean run''s tabs, each Claude CLI resuming its session on its login, then reselects the person and tab (M.ORCH-T862); b3b1dfe9 Add the session-restore file''s model and store, and learn each terminal tab''s Claude session: RestoreState/RestoreTab, SessionRestoreStore (atomic temp-then-move writes, rotation keeping the last 5 runs'' files, ReopenRequest building a tab''s claude --resume reopen from its PaneRequest), and TerminalsViewModel.Update matchin