out (M.ORCH-T988); df6d6b21 Bound the gateway''s login throttle and make it O(1) and race-safe: one short lock, each address keeps only its last five failure times, at most 4096 addresses with the longest-quiet one forgotten first, an IPv6 address counted by its /64, and POST /auth/token counts an attempt before checking the key (TryBegin) and takes it back on success, so a flood of addresses can''t grow memory or make every failure scan the table, and concurrent guesses can''t slip past the five-try limit (M.ORCH-T987); 382c05a9 Keep the gateway''s last good acl.json and broadcast.json when a read fails just now, and retry: TermGatewayAudit.TryReadAcl and TermBroadcast.TryRead tell a transient I/O failure from a missing or invalid file, AclGrants and BroadcastFile take the new stamp only once a read succeeds, and TermBroadcast.Update never writes a change over settings it couldn''t read, so one sharing violation no longer locks members out or unshares every session until the file next changes (M.ORCH-T986); 844a503b Clean the viewer-supplied ViewerId before it reaches a log line: TermProtocol.LogSafeId drops control and format characters and caps it at 64 characters, TermHost logs only that, and the gateway forwards a remote viewer''s Hello with its id cleaned, so no viewer can forge host log lines with embedded newlines (M.ORCH-T990); c7259581 Make orchestrator gateway revoke --session match the session id in any case, as the gateway does: grants store the id in lower case, and revoke compares LOWER(session), so a revoke typed in another case no longer reports no such grant while it stays in force (M.ORCH-T989); 62a49020 Judge an app presence by its pid and that process''s start time against when the presence was said, not by pid alone: a presence the hub kept from an app long gone no longer counts once its pid is reused by a later process, so open-ticket starts Tickets.Desktop instead of going to nobody; one with no time of its own is still judged by pid (M.ORCH-