INSERT INTO tickets (id, repo, number, date, type, status, summary, ref, ordinal, row_md) VALUES ('M.ORCH-T1063', 'MindAttic.Orchestrator', 1063, '2026-10-26', 'fix', 'closed', 'Fails on main: MindAttic.Orchestrator.Tests.GatewayTests.A_revoked_grant_closes_the_stream_it_allowed — System.OperationCanceledException : The operation was canceled. (landed on main since the last green run: tickets M.ORCH-T1042, M.ORCH-T1006, M.ORCH-T1061, M.ORCH-T1057, M.ORCH-T1056, M.ORCH-T1052, M.ORCH-T1050, M.ORCH-T1049, M.ORCH-T1048, M.ORCH-T1041, M.ORCH-T1039, M.ORCH-T1038, M.ORCH-T1016, M.ORCH-T1028, M.ORCH-T1040, M.ORCH-T1035, M.ORCH-T1034, M.ORCH-T1033, M.ORCH-T1027, M.ORCH-T1026, M.ORCH-T1025, M.ORCH-T1024 in 359eaffd Update the stale BusyClisTests case to M.ORCH-T1042''s rule: a subagent mark naming no CLI or an unreadable state still refuses a deploy while every open CLI is hosted (an unhosted CLI the scan missed may own it), and an unreadable state is dropped only when its session is a hosted CLI''s own; the test still asserted M.ORCH-T1006''s since-reversed drop (M.ORCH-T1061); bccf0333 ï»¿Schedule Psst renewal reminders when orchestrator gateway token mints a 365-day member token: psst remind at 09:00 local 30, 14, 7, 5, 3, 2 and 1 days before expiry, named per member and lead time so re-minting replaces them; --minutes tokens get none (M.ORCH-T1057); 1ff7a42a Gateway member tokens minted by ''orchestrator gateway token'' last 365 days (a ''member'' kind in the payload, validated up to 365 days); session tokens keep their 60-minute cap, and revoking grants or replacing the signing key still cuts any token off at once (M.ORCH-T1056); 607e1905 Guard the context gate''s PostToolUse state save so a failed write can''t raise a hook error on a CLI''s tool call (M.ORCH-T1052); 9babfeba Fold a fallback TermViewer at once when its link is replaced while the dashboard is present: since T1040 it stopped reconnecting only once dashboardSeen was set (two presence looks, 2-4s, or a bus presence), so a dashboard reattaching to a protocol-1 host first ping-ponged the single-viewer session with it for a few seconds. Its reconnect probe and OnDetached now also look at DashboardPresence.IsPresent (the dashboard''s single-instance mutex or show event exists) and fold (M.ORCH-T1050); e70dc9f3 Never send the start of a Vault value bare: since T1038 a Vault value''s first 8-11 characters were a weak masker candidate, sent as they were after their 500ms hold or at a flush, so a real secret printed with a gap leaked up to half of itself to remote viewers. Any held start of a Vault value is now strong, masked when its hold runs out, at a flush, and even by a final call; weak candidates such as apiKey = getT still go as they are (M.ORCH-T1049); 5c99472a Let a Stop hook cut off after its deciding save read idle to every reader: ContextCycler.Read now applies the 75s deciding-staleness rule (IsBusyTurn) as BusyClis and LiveSessions do, so AllocateWaker, Allocate.ByHand and LimitWaker no longer see that CLI working for good; the hook pops deciding in its PostToolUse and Notification saves, and its final save can no longer raise (M.ORCH-T1048); cb7b7e3d Let a remote stream outlive its token with an in-band refresh: since T983 every gateway stream was cut when its bearer token expired and audited as "access revoked", since a WebSocket can''t present a new token. A viewer may now send a RefreshToken frame (0x20, never forwarded to a host) carrying a fresh token; the gateway validates it as it did the attach token (signature, lifetime, the same member, at least the stream''s access), and the stream then lasts as long as it does; refused ones are logged and audited (at most five per stream). A lapse is closed and audited as "token expired"; a replaced signing key still closes the stream at the next check as "access revoked". The team wall''s and the pop-out viewer''s streams (WebSocketFrameStream via GatewayClient) look at the member''s token in the settings every 20s and send any newer one for the same gateway, so a token renewed with gateway remote add keeps open tiles running (M.ORCH-T1041); 34668fed Close two remote-stream masking gaps left by T982: a Replay was masked with final:true, so a token half-printed when a viewer attached went out bare up to the replay''s end; it is now masked as a held candidate whose hold ran out (StreamMasker.ProcessReplay), and the rest of it masked as live output goes on. And once a held candidate''s start was masked, a short value (a password after password:) that then failed the 16-character LooksRandom test stopped being a candidate and its remainder went out bare; a run whose start was masked unfinished is now masked to its end, across a wrap''s break, and no further (M.ORCH-T1039); 31a875e0 Stop the remote-stream masker bulleting ordinary code: since T982 any value after key/token/secret/password with one digit or capital (key=1, apiKey = getT) or the first 8 characters of a Vault value was a candidate, masked for good once its 500ms hold ran out or on any non-Output frame, such as the frequent Modes frames. Candidates are now weak or strong: key=1 and other short digit runs aren''t held at all; a code-like value and a Vault value''s first few characters are only held, in case the rest makes a match, then sent as they are; only a begun token shape, a value after a password name, a value after another name of 8+ characters with digits and letters, or 12+ characters (or half) of a Vault value is masked unfinished. Modes, Size and other non-content frames now pass a held candidate as a Title does; only Exit flushes it (M.ORCH-T1038); 226b4522 Close the session pipe when the gateway''s WebSocket upgrade fails: the pipe opened for a stream was disposed only inside TermBridge.RunAsync, so an AcceptWebSocketAsync that threw left it open, leaking a handle per failed upgrade and a half-open viewer on the host; it is now disposed before the failure goes on to the contained 500 (M.ORCH-T1016); 2e7a87b7 Restart the team gateway onto a newer install after a redeploy: GatewaySupervisor kept a managed gateway running for as long as its settings matched, so an old build (say, one whose masker leaks secrets) kept serving remote viewers and its version folder was never cleaned up. The gateway''s status now names its exe; each tick the supervisor compares it (or, for an older gateway, its process''s main module, then its version) with the exe it would start now, the newest under GatewayInstalls, and restarts it there when they differ; remote viewers reconnect (M.ORCH-T1028); a38adcd4 Let fallback TermViewer windows reconnect while the dashboard is absent: since T976 they got no liveness probe, so a passing pipe drop with the dashboard down left the window detached, holding the slot mutex and dropping keys. They now reconnect while the host lives and the dashboard''s presence hasn''t been seen; once it is, the probe says no and the window folds as before (M.ORCH-T1040); a46d5294 Treat a registry read failure as unknown, not gone, when a dropped relay asks whether its host lives: TermSessions.Get returned null when a read failed, so a passing antivirus or indexer hold marked the tab ended for good (and closing it killed a live CLI). TermSessions.TryGet tells the two apart, as Enumerate does since T995, and HostAlive then asks the host''s process (M.ORCH-T1035); 1f572d64 Report a failed kill and keep its tab: TermHostKill swallowed a kill that failed (an elevated host), so the tab went while the host lived and the resync re-added it later. Kill now says whether the host is gone; a tab close that couldn''t end it keeps the tab with a toast, End CLI keeps the viewer with a status, and a Started message for a session closed here lately no longer gets a tab back (M.ORCH-T1034); 03b6ae72 Unregister a killed host from the killer: closing a tab or End CLI hard-kills the host tree, so Registration.End never ran, no ended went on the bus and the registry file lingered until a reader pruned it. After a successful kill TermHostKill now waits (off the caller''s thread, up to 2s) for the host to go, deletes its registry file and announces ended (M.ORCH-T1033); d1296b2d Collapse the API credit burndown card until there is a spend reading, as the utilization card does: the API-key tab showed a blank card with a null chart and an accessible name ending in a bare colon (M.ORCH-T1027); 1ca0c44a Name the CLI tab''s shared glyph for screen readers: TerminalSharedGlyph had only a tooltip, so a screen reader read a private-use glyph and the shared state was lost; it gets an AutomationProperties.Name like its watched sibling (M.ORCH-T1026); 798638ca Bring the selected person tab into view: the horizontally scrolled login strip never followed the selection, so Ctrl+Tab, Show who''s working or an org switch could select a tab left off screen. The selected tab''s container is brought into view after each selection or strip change (M.ORCH-T1025); f71c811f Tell the CLI tab strip its selection stands after a Ctrl+click: PersonTerminalsViewModel.SelectedPane ignored the null write without raising PropertyChanged, so the strip showed nothing chosen while the terminal stayed shown. It now re-raises once the binding''s write is done; the login tab strip''s StripSelection does the same (M.ORCH-T1024))', 'passes on main@f406eed', 1062, NULL);
INSERT INTO tickets (id, repo, number, date, type, status, summary, ref, ordinal, row_md) VALUES ('M.ORCH-T1064', 'MindAttic.Orchestrator', 1064, '2026-10-26', 'fix', 'closed', 'Fails on main: MindAttic.Orchestrator.Tests.GatewayTests.A_stream_ends_when_its_token_expires — System.OperationCanceledException : The operation was canceled. (landed on main since the last green run: tickets M.ORCH-T1042, M.ORCH-T1006, M.ORCH-T1061, M.ORCH-T1057, M.ORCH-T1056, M.ORCH-T1052, M.ORCH-T1050, M.ORCH-T1049, M.ORCH-T1048, M.ORCH-T1041, M.ORCH-T1039, M.ORCH-T1038, M.ORCH-T1016, M.ORCH-T1028, M.ORCH-T1040, M.ORCH-T1035, M.ORCH-T1034, M.ORCH-T1033, M.ORCH-T1027, M.ORCH-T1026, M.ORCH-T1025, M.ORCH-T1024 in 359eaffd Update the stale BusyClisTests case to M.ORCH-T1042''s rule: a subagent mark naming no CLI or an unreadable state still refuses a deploy while every open CLI is hosted (an unhosted CLI the scan missed may own it), and an unreadable state is dropped only when its session is a hosted CLI''s own; the test still asserted M.ORCH-T1006''s since-reversed drop (M.ORCH-T1061); bccf0333 ï»¿Schedule Psst renewal reminders when orchestrator gateway token mints a 365-day member token: psst remind at 09:00 local 30, 14, 7, 5, 3, 2 and 1 days before expiry, named per member and lead time so re-minting replaces them; --minutes tokens get none (M.ORCH-T1057); 1ff7a42a Gateway member tokens minted by ''orchestrator gateway token'' last 365 days (a ''member'' kind in the payload, validated up to 365 days); session tokens keep their 60-minute cap, and revoking grants or replacing the signing key still cuts any token off at once (M.ORCH-T1056); 607e1905 Guard the context gate''s PostToolUse state save so a failed write can''t raise a hook error on a CLI''s tool call (M.ORCH-T1052); 9babfeba Fold a fallback TermViewer at once when its link is replaced while the dashboard is present: since T1040 it stopped reconnecting only once dashboardSeen was set (two presence looks, 2-4s, or a bus presence), so a dashboard reattaching to a protocol-1 host first ping-ponged the single-viewer session with it for a few seconds. Its reconnect probe and OnDetached now also look at DashboardPresence.IsPresent (the dashboard''s single-instance mutex or show event exists) and fold (M.ORCH-T1050); e70dc9f3 Never send the start of a Vault value bare: since T1038 a Vault value''s first 8-11 characters were a weak masker candidate, sent as they were after their 500ms hold or at a flush, so a real secret printed with a gap leaked up to half of itself to remote viewers. Any held start of a Vault value is now strong, masked when its hold runs out, at a flush, and even by a final call; weak candidates such as apiKey = getT still go as they are (M.ORCH-T1049); 5c99472a Let a Stop hook cut off after its deciding save read idle to every reader: ContextCycler.Read now applies the 75s deciding-staleness rule (IsBusyTurn) as BusyClis and LiveSessions do, so AllocateWaker, Allocate.ByHand and LimitWaker no longer see that CLI working for good; the hook pops deciding in its PostToolUse and Notification saves, and its final save can no longer raise (M.ORCH-T1048); cb7b7e3d Let a remote stream outlive its token with an in-band refresh: since T983 every gateway stream was cut when its bearer token expired and audited as "access revoked", since a WebSocket can''t present a new token. A viewer may now send a RefreshToken frame (0x20, never forwarded to a host) carrying a fresh token; the gateway validates it as it did the attach token (signature, lifetime, the same member, at least the stream''s access), and the stream then lasts as long as it does; refused ones are logged and audited (at most five per stream). A lapse is closed and audited as "token expired"; a replaced signing key still closes the stream at the next check as "access revoked". The team wall''s and the pop-out viewer''s streams (WebSocketFrameStream via GatewayClient) look at the member''s token in the settings every 20s and send any newer one for the same gateway, so a token renewed with gateway remote add keeps open tiles running (M.ORCH-T1041); 34668fed Close two remote-stream masking gaps left by T982: a Replay was masked with final:true, so a token half-printed when a viewer attached went out bare up to the replay''s end; it is now masked as a held candidate whose hold ran out (StreamMasker.ProcessReplay), and the rest of it masked as live output goes on. And once a held candidate''s start was masked, a short value (a password after password:) that then failed the 16-character LooksRandom test stopped being a candidate and its remainder went out bare; a run whose start was masked unfinished is now masked to its end, across a wrap''s break, and no further (M.ORCH-T1039); 31a875e0 Stop the remote-stream masker bulleting ordinary code: since T982 any value after key/token/secret/password with one digit or capital (key=1, apiKey = getT) or the first 8 characters of a Vault value was a candidate, masked for good once its 500ms hold ran out or on any non-Output frame, such as the frequent Modes frames. Candidates are now weak or strong: key=1 and other short digit runs aren''t held at all; a code-like value and a Vault value''s first few characters are only held, in case the rest makes a match, then sent as they are; only a begun token shape, a value after a password name, a value after another name of 8+ characters with digits and letters, or 12+ characters (or half) of a Vault value is masked unfinished. Modes, Size and other non-content frames now pass a held candidate as a Title does; only Exit flushes it (M.ORCH-T1038); 226b4522 Close the session pipe when the gateway''s WebSocket upgrade fails: the pipe opened for a stream was disposed only inside TermBridge.RunAsync, so an AcceptWebSocketAsync that threw left it open, leaking a handle per failed upgrade and a half-open viewer on the host; it is now disposed before the failure goes on to the contained 500 (M.ORCH-T1016); 2e7a87b7 Restart the team gateway onto a newer install after a redeploy: GatewaySupervisor kept a managed gateway running for as long as its settings matched, so an old build (say, one whose masker leaks secrets) kept serving remote viewers and its version folder was never cleaned up. The gateway''s status now names its exe; each tick the supervisor compares it (or, for an older gateway, its process''s main module, then its version) with the exe it would start now, the newest under GatewayInstalls, and restarts it there when they differ; remote viewers reconnect (M.ORCH-T1028); a38adcd4 Let fallback TermViewer windows reconnect while the dashboard is absent: since T976 they got no liveness probe, so a passing pipe drop with the dashboard down left the window detached, holding the slot mutex and dropping keys. They now reconnect while the host lives and the dashboard''s presence hasn''t been seen; once it is, the probe says no and the window folds as before (M.ORCH-T1040); a46d5294 Treat a registry read failure as unknown, not gone, when a dropped relay asks whether its host lives: TermSessions.Get returned null when a read failed, so a passing antivirus or indexer hold marked the tab ended for good (and closing it killed a live CLI). TermSessions.TryGet tells the two apart, as Enumerate does since T995, and HostAlive then asks the host''s process (M.ORCH-T1035); 1f572d64 Report a failed kill and keep its tab: TermHostKill swallowed a kill that failed (an elevated host), so the tab went while the host lived and the resync re-added it later. Kill now says whether the host is gone; a tab close that couldn''t end it keeps the tab with a toast, End CLI keeps the viewer with a status, and a Started message for a session closed here lately no longer gets a tab back (M.ORCH-T1034); 03b6ae72 Unregister a killed host from the killer: closing a tab or End CLI hard-kills the host tree, so Registration.End never ran, no ended went on the bus and the registry file lingered until a reader pruned it. After a successful kill TermHostKill now waits (off the caller''s thread, up to 2s) for the host to go, deletes its registry file and announces ended (M.ORCH-T1033); d1296b2d Collapse the API credit burndown card until there is a spend reading, as the utilization card does: the API-key tab showed a blank card with a null chart and an accessible name ending in a bare colon (M.ORCH-T1027); 1ca0c44a Name the CLI tab''s shared glyph for screen readers: TerminalSharedGlyph had only a tooltip, so a screen reader read a private-use glyph and the shared state was lost; it gets an AutomationProperties.Name like its watched sibling (M.ORCH-T1026); 798638ca Bring the selected person tab into view: the horizontally scrolled login strip never followed the selection, so Ctrl+Tab, Show who''s working or an org switch could select a tab left off screen. The selected tab''s container is brought into view after each selection or strip change (M.ORCH-T1025); f71c811f Tell the CLI tab strip its selection stands after a Ctrl+click: PersonTerminalsViewModel.SelectedPane ignored the null write without raising PropertyChanged, so the strip showed nothing chosen while the terminal stayed shown. It now re-raises once the binding''s write is done; the login tab strip''s StripSelection does the same (M.ORCH-T1024))', 'passes on main@f406eed', 1063, NULL);
