INSERT INTO ticket_notes (seq, ticket_id, author, at, markdown) VALUES (1, 'U.HARE-T54', 'ryand', '2026-10-26T04:52:58Z', 'From U.HARE-T52 (7d24220): leaving the arena past the 400 px buffer zone (LeaveArena command) currently costs a life only on the ship (PlayerHealth out-of-bounds path / ShipHealth). When this ticket wires LIVES into the session, route that out-of-bounds loss through the same session lives so both deaths count the same.');
INSERT INTO ticket_notes (seq, ticket_id, author, at, markdown) VALUES (2, 'U.OVW-T15', 'ryand', '2026-10-26T07:07:20Z', 'RESUME, don''t restart: an earlier run (stopped by the cool-off) left uncommitted work in D:\Projects\MindAttic.worktrees\Unity.Overworld\U.OVW-T15. Done: Core/Content/RestTuning.cs + heroes.json ''rest'' section via HeroData; Hero sleep hours + arrow-repeat timer; PartyCommands Rest command + kneel/lay/stand and hours-changed events; Party rest-key cycle (refused in battle) and arrows set hours while laid; WorldClock internal SetHour/Advance; Core/Heroes/SleepCycle.cs (Sleep, SleepUntil; fade 5/tick; on black restore hours x 1/8 of max HP/MP and AP unless poisoned, VB banker''s rounding, capped; clock advances; fade back in). LEFT: hud.json/HudData ''Rest for N hour(s)?'' text + HudPresenter; WorldViewPresenter dims by the fade; HeroInput binds \ to rest, Enter/left-click while laid to sleep; OverworldBootstrap install order party->sleep->clock and scripted args -overworld-rest <kneel|lay|hours>[,s] and -overworld-sleep-until <hour>[,s]; Core RestTests + an EditMode test; headless build (.meta files); muted captures; BIBLE rows: (1) Moon Berry/Morningstar now wake at 10 PM/5 AM (original woke an hour late, 11 PM/6 AM, by setting the clock then adding the sleep hour), (2) story A14 maps the items'' scripts onto SleepUntil and A13 runs them; then commit, rebase, push, close, and mark story U.OVW-US-A11 done.');
INSERT INTO ticket_notes (seq, ticket_id, author, at, markdown) VALUES (3, 'U.RICO-T26', 'ryand', '2026-10-26T07:41:59Z', 'Follow-up: the fog''s look and reveal rules were invented (5-unit circle) because the GML source was thought missing; it exists under R:\...\GameMaker\gmlricochet\Ricochet.gmx. A fix ticket ports the original''s obj_fogscreen/obj_fog/obj_fogofwar_emitter/reset_fogofwar.');
INSERT INTO ticket_notes (seq, ticket_id, author, at, markdown) VALUES (4, 'U.RICO-T43', 'ryand', '2026-10-26T08:14:57Z', 'RESUME, don''t restart: branch orch/u.rico-t43 in D:\Projects\MindAttic.worktrees\Unity.Ricochet\U.RICO-T43 has c817242 (Core: pause freezes clock, Ready hold, crates, hazards, shots, driving; refuses actions except votes/join/leave; Reroll level before first shot; Quit round; Tests/Core.Tests/PauseTests.cs, 81 Core tests pass) and cbb4d12 WIP, NOT yet compiled in Unity (pause synced to peers; clock/Ready/input/shot freeze per peer; AI waits; Runtime/ArenaPause.cs host pause/resume/reroll/quit + pause/resume/quit-round votes with VoteMenu wording; Runtime/PauseMenu.cs Resume/Reroll(host, before first shot)/Music toggle/Vote to quit, hooked into MatchHud; GameAudio.SetMusicMuted saves only real profile values and stays silent under the CLI session mute; Esc-menu ''Pause the game'' button; Pause key moved to P / Pause / right-stick press, menu.json controls row, GameDataTests+MenuFlowTests updated). LEFT: 1) write Assets/Ricochet/Tests/PlayMode/PauseMenuTests.cs (host pause freezes every peer, AI waits, guest pause/resume as votes, host-only reroll, quit round as a vote, Music toggle under session mute); 2) headless Unity compile (.meta for ArenaPause.cs, PauseMenu.cs, PauseMenuTests.cs), run EditMode GameInputTests and PlayMode PauseMenuTests, ReadyCardTests, ProfileTests; 3) BIBLE/RECONSTRUCTION deviations: Pause off Esc, music button = on/off toggle not Next Track, Quit round = vote dropping to practice not setup screen; 4) squash WIP commit, rebase onto origin/main (U.RICO-T77 fog landed 06983f8), push, close.');
INSERT INTO ticket_notes (seq, ticket_id, author, at, markdown) VALUES (5, 'U.HARE-T21', 'ryand', '2026-10-26T08:19:59Z', 'Research from an aborted run (no code written yet; worktree untouched): most stage-mode data already exists from U.HARE-T52: room_sidescroll 12000x1080 with bg_tropicalocean tiled horizontally only, room_shaft 1920x12000 with bg_stormclouds tiled both ways; their camera/minimap view settings; per-level wrap flags (level 4 shaft: wraps both axes, no random_positions on wrap; level 5 side-scroll: wraps horizontally, randomizes on wrap); ArenaWorld.CheckPlayer already applies wrap and out-of-bounds. Confirmed differences from the open arena in the room files: camera follows with no 40 px/step limit; minimap port at 1300,860 not 1600,800 (both already in data); both stage rooms pre-place a player object at 1362,1098 in the room itself (open arena leaves it to setup_level) - check how the rebuild handles that; room_sidescroll also places obj_surface_reflection (that''s U.HARE-T58, not this ticket). LEFT: read level_04, level_05, setup_level, reset_player, random_positions, obj_spawnpoint and obj_game for stage-specific spawn/respawn/400 px buffer rules and the pre-placed player; build only those differences on ArenaWorld/ArenaRoom; Core + PlayMode tests; BIBLE deviations; headless compile; land.');
INSERT INTO ticket_notes (seq, ticket_id, author, at, markdown) VALUES (6, 'U.HARE-T81', 'ryand', '2026-10-26T08:27:20Z', 'Not reproducible on main (84ba37f): ArenaRoomPlayTests.TheArenaRenders with -Graphics (worktree U.HARE-T81, Screenshots/arena.png) shows the rocks drawn correctly with the spr_rock textures and outlines, grey. The whole main view is uniformly dimmed at the 0.5 s capture (the level fade-in/banner), which the minimap camera doesn''t get, so minimap rocks look lighter. No ''rotated patches of earth background'' appear; U.HARE-T57''s description was a misread of the dimmed frame.');
INSERT INTO ticket_notes (seq, ticket_id, author, at, markdown) VALUES (7, 'U.RICO-T43', 'ryand', '2026-10-26T08:30:00Z', 'Progress (2nd aborted run): branch orch/u.rico-t43 rebased onto origin/main incl. U.RICO-T77 fog (06983f8), no conflicts; now 8173ba1 (Core pause rules, Reroll, Quit round, PauseTests) + 19b63eb (WIP, still NOT compiled in Unity). Worktree clean. PauseMenuTests.cs not started. Reuse: TestMatches.cs Begin + WithoutReadyCard/StockReadyCard; vote tests'' VoteBoard.RegisterPrefab(session) in OnSessionsCreated, then VoteBoard.Spawn(Server) and board.AddKind(arena.CreatePauseVote()/Resume/QuitRound), passing 2-of-2 with client StartVote + host CastVote(true) (see Arena.RouteVote); SessionMuteAudioTests'' TempProfiles.Use() + Profiles.SessionMuted=true for the Music toggle. Remaining steps unchanged (note 4: tests, headless compile + .meta, test run, BIBLE deviations, squash, rebase, push, close).');
INSERT INTO ticket_notes (seq, ticket_id, author, at, markdown) VALUES (8, 'U.RICO-T44', 'ryand', '2026-10-26T09:20:48Z', 'Research from an aborted run (no code yet; worktree clean): (1) Source choice open: Ricochet.gmx has 314 sprite / 63 background files on disk but its project lists only 275 / 50; RECONSTRUCTION''s 315/64 counts come from R:\Projects\_PRE_2022\_PRE_2021\_PRE_2020\_PRE_2017\gmlRicochet\09-05-13_2.20am (same layout) - compare the two; import every file on disk and flag whether it''s in the project file (unlike Hare, which skips unlisted). (2) Fonts in Ricochet.gmx: fnt_impact, fnt_score, fnt_score_shadow, fnt_mono, fnt_small, fnt_count, fnt_credits, font4, font5 (only impact/score/mono/small/count in the project); no font_add_sprite call, so the ''sprite font'' is probably fnt_score_shadow or from the older copy. (3) draw_text_outline = text in black at every offset within the outline size, then white on top; 130 calls, almost all size 1. (4) Mirror Hare''s pipeline (tools/import-gml-art.ps1 + gml-json.ps1 -> gml-art.json; GmlArtImporter/GmlArtBuilder -> import settings, clips, atlases, manifest; import-gml-fonts.ps1 + GmlFontBuilder from GameMaker glyph atlases) but fonts must be TMP_FontAsset for uGUI/TMP; TMP outline needs SDF, so either generate an SDF atlas or draw the outline the original way. (5) No .gitattributes in Ricochet; git-lfs 3.7.1 installed - add LFS rules for the new art folders. (6) Scope: tank art/tracks are U.RICO-T45, backgrounds/clouds/borders/shapes are U.RICO-T46 - this ticket = import + catalogue + fonts + swaps for the most visible pieces (HUD fonts, shots, crates), follow-up for the rest.');
INSERT INTO ticket_notes (seq, ticket_id, author, at, markdown) VALUES (9, 'U.HARE-T22', 'ryand', '2026-10-26T09:27:41Z', 'RESUME, don''t restart. Local WIP commit on orch/u.hare-t22 (DOES NOT COMPILE yet: ShipFlight emits a ShipLeaving event that doesn''t exist). Original behaviour (HARE.gmx obj_level_results, set_level_complete, obj_player leave state): set_level_complete makes obj_level_results at (960,270) and pauses; panel spr_results 712x712 origin 356,0 at 0.7 alpha; white 1px-outlined text: ''Level Complete'' fnt_score y+25, ''Time'' + healthbar.strTime y+125, ''Enemies Killed'' + KILLS y+150, ''Press [ENTER] to continue'' centred y+331. Enter: unpause, ship leave state with exit_x = current x, invulnerable, sfx_boost, white ring size 1 at the ship, panel goes. Leaving: turn 3 deg/step toward a point above the room top, leap art, 2x flight speed, black smoke-up (size 0) + orange smoke (size 1) 36 px behind; once y < -sprite_height: score -> 0, level +1, setup_level (removes panel). The original never returns to room_map after a level - record that deviation in the BIBLE and that U.HARE-T19/T26 wire the map. DONE: Core/Arena/LevelResults.cs (data, layout, HudClock ''00:00'' counted per room, never reset by a level); ArenaTuning results settings + validation + GameContent.json; FlightTuning Leaving state + 360 deg/s turn; ShipFlight velocity for leaving + Leave()/AimExit()/steering/turn-direction port. LEFT: 1) ShipLeaving event in PlayerEvents.cs; Step() runs the steering while leaving. 2) Core LeaveLevel command (permanent invulnerability until reset), AimExit command, leap pose while leaving, leave smoke puffs in ShipLook drawn by PlayerLook. 3) PlayerShipController: send exit angle each step while leaving, set velocity while leaving, freeze the ship while paused but not leaving. 4) ArenaRoom: LevelResultsView (UI Toolkit, like LevelStartView) on the level-completed event; Enter via an ad-hoc input action like StartupRoom; count HudClock each elapsed second; skip the out-of-bounds check while leaving; above the room -> advance level with score reset, set up next level or change room reusing OnLevelAdvance; remove the panel in Begin. 5) Kill counting on enemy death by the player (finishes BIBLE D11). 6) Core LevelResultsTests + a PlayMode results test, BIBLE + RECONSTRUCTION, compile with tools/unity.ps1, squash the WIP, rebase, push, close.');
INSERT INTO ticket_notes (seq, ticket_id, author, at, markdown) VALUES (10, 'U.OVW-T18', 'ryand', '2026-10-26T09:33:19Z', 'Plan from an aborted run (no code yet; worktree clean), from Script.vb + frmMain.vb: one Core/Scripts ScriptInterpreter implementing IScriptRunner, replacing both ItemScripts and CurrencyScripts (Pickups.cs), wired in OverworldBootstrap where ItemScripts is; keep ItemScripts behaviour/tests (draught LAYDOWN + TIME HOUR -> SleepUntil; lowering a vital floors at 0). Console: ConsoleKey(player,keyName,shift) command copying the scripter keys - ~ toggles; Insert recalls last + opens; Enter runs, remembers, closes; Esc/F11 close; C on empty line types ''CHANGE '', again ''CHANGE CAMERA ''; +/= gives ''+'' or ''='' with Shift; other keys append their key name; prompt ''/ > text|'' alternating ''\ > text '' blinking every 0.5 s at (55,75) in (128,255,128). While console open or a script runs, the party ignores that player''s input; running scripts end at their target (BIBLE fix); console keys stay live while a script runs. Errors via the message board: ''Script failed to execute.'' (error) / ''Script failed to run.'' (exception); an item stays in the pack when its script fails. CHANGE BOOK / CHANGE OPTIONS only record settings until A16 / A20 draw them; quest end scripts (only CHANGE TIME HOUR 18 today) called by A15. Original bugs to fix + BIBLE: a command not 4 or 2 words reused the previous command''s words (empty Enter re-ran the last item effect); RUN NIGHT skipped later commands; CHANGE TIME HOUR +n did nothing; CHANGE LIGHT crashed on negatives and on ''128,128,128''; CHANGE CURSOR POS CENTER no effect; CHANGE ENEMY HEALTH never matched; Shift stuck on for the session. LEFT: everything - Core code, hud.json, Unity console + HUD wiring, tests, BIBLE, headless compile, muted capture, land, close, story done.');
INSERT INTO ticket_notes (seq, ticket_id, author, at, markdown) VALUES (11, 'U.RICO-T45', 'ryand', '2026-10-26T10:39:43Z', 'Git LFS: since U.RICO-T44 (ee2d01c) Ricochet stores PNG art in LFS (.gitattributes), but the repo has no LFS pre-push hook (its hooks dir is custom). Before ''git push origin HEAD:main'' run ''git lfs push origin HEAD'' (or ''git lfs install'' once in the worktree), then check ''git lfs ls-files'' shows the new art and the push uploaded the objects - otherwise main gets pointer files with no content.');
