INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 13, 'backlog', '83', '1. Brainstorm: one naming theme for Orchestrator, Workflow, /autopilot (/work), /throttle, /unthrottle, /crossrepo and Launcher (triggers: workflow is a reserved keyword in Windows PowerShell 5.1, and the names come from different worlds). Leading idea, railway: Conductor (Orchestrator), Tickets (Workflow; CLI becomes ''tickets new''), crew (subagents), line (repo), car (worktree), /all-aboard and /last-stop (autopilot on/off), /throttle kept, /express (unthrottle), /transfer (crossrepo), Station (Launcher). Alternatives: aviation (Tower, Logbook, /clearance, Hangar); racing (PitWall, TimingSheet, /race, /pace-car, /green-flag, /open-track, Garage); everyday driving (ECU, Logbook, /floor-it, /off-road, Ignition); mission control (MissionControl, Manifest, /orbit, /coast, /full-burn, /spacewalk, LaunchPad); orchestra (keep Orchestrator, Score, /perform, /adagio, /allegro, /ensemble, Stage); military (CommandCenter, Orders, /campaign, /hold-fire, /full-assault, /joint-ops, Barracks); kitchen (expediter, order rail, /simmer, /rush); beehive, film set, harbor. Open questions: new project codes (M.FLOW would move), PowerShell 7 avoids the keyword clash anyway.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 14, 'story', '695', '- **M.TIX-US-C1 🟡** As an Agent, `/commit` logs each commit through `workflow ticket` instead of
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 15, 'story', '696', '- **M.TIX-US-C2 🟡** As a Dev, the Launcher has a Workflow menu item showing open tickets and repo
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 16, 'story', '697', '- **M.TIX-US-C3 ⬜** As a Dev, `workflow codes fix` renames a duplicate project code and its ticket
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 17, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 18, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 19, 'epic', 'D', '## Epic D — The database: safety, concurrency and git');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 20, 'story', '1047', '- **M.TIX-US-D1 ⬜** As a Dev, `workflow db restore` rebuilds data/workflow.db from the committed data/workflow.sql dump and proves it matches (row counts per table, `db check` clean, every view renders unchanged), so a corrupt or merge-conflicted binary is never data loss (M.FLOW-LAW-3). Today nothing reads the dump back.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 21, 'story', '1048', '- **M.TIX-US-D2 ⬜** As an Agent, my feature commits never carry data/workflow.db or data/workflow.sql; only `workflow db sync` commits them, and .gitattributes marks the db binary with a merge that keeps the working copy, so merging a worktree branch can''t conflict on the database or roll it back to an older snapshot. Today ordinary commits sweep it in whenever it''s modified.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 22, 'story', '1049', '- **M.TIX-US-D3 ⬜** As an Agent running alongside other autopilot agents, `workflow ticket new` from many processes at once hands out distinct IDs with none lost and no ''database is locked'' failure, proved by a test that starts parallel writers against one database (and decides whether WAL beats today''s journal_mode=DELETE with a 15s busy_timeout).');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 23, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 24, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 25, 'epic', 'E', '## Epic E — CLI output and coverage');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 26, 'story', '1050', '- **M.TIX-US-E1 ⬜** As an Agent, workflow output piped or redirected (not a terminal) has no ANSI escape codes and honors NO_COLOR, so scripts and agents read plain text. Today `ticket list | cat` prints raw color codes around ''0 ticket(s)'', and help text keeps its underline codes even with NO_COLOR.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 27, 'story', '1051', '- **M.TIX-US-E2 ⬜** As a Dev, `workflow story list` is readable in an 80-column terminal: one line per story with ID, glyph, epic and the text cut to fit, instead of today''s 20-character Story column that wraps each story over seven lines. `--json` is unchanged.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 28, 'story', '1052', '- **M.TIX-US-E3 ⬜** As a Dev, `workflow ticket list --search <text>` matches ID, summary and ref (case-insensitive) across the workspace, so finding a ticket doesn''t mean piping --json through grep.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 29, 'story', '1053', '- **M.TIX-US-E4 ⬜** As a Dev, the commands agents run that have no CLI test yet are tested through the real `workflow` on a temp workspace: story new/edit/status, epic new, backlog add, ticket link (a refused cycle), ticket correct, db render, and db sync --no-push committing only the database files.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 30, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 31, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 32, 'epic', 'F', '## Epic F — Viewer and canon');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 33, 'story', '1054', '- **M.TIX-US-F1 ⬜** As a Dev, `workflow view` shows each ticket''s and story''s links (requires, blocks) and a ticket''s history, and an ID in a summary or ref links to that item, so I can see from the page why something is blocked.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 34, 'story', '1055', '- **M.TIX-US-F2 ⬜** As a Dev, the Launcher''s Workflow menu (M.LNCH-US-E6) has an ''Open viewer'' item that runs `workflow view`, scoped to the repo I''m in.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 35, 'story', '1056', '- **M.TIX-US-F3 ⬜** As an Agent reading the canon, README.md and docs/BIBLE.md describe the database, not the markdown era: the intro and architecture diagrams say tickets live in SQLite, `ticket new` no longer claims ''only that one line changes'', ''stories are still written by hand'' goes, the glossary''s ''Ticket log'' stops pointing at the ## Tickets table, M.FLOW-LAW-2 stops repeating its trigger sentence, and the codex doctor passes.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 36, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 37, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 38, 'epic', 'G', '## Epic G — Desktop UI (Workflow Desktop, WPF, WCAG 2.2 AA)');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 39, 'story', '1071', '- **M.TIX-US-G1 ⬜** As a Dev, Workflow Desktop (src/MindAttic.Workflow.Desktop, WPF on net10.0-windows with MindAttic.Components.Wpf, the Orchestrator''s look) opens from a Desktop and Start-menu shortcut that shows assets/logo.ico, which is also the exe and window icon, installed by deploy.ps1 to C:\Apps\MindAttic.Workflow.Desktop.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 40, 'story', '1072', '- **M.TIX-US-G2 ⬜** As a Dev or Agent, a ticket''s approval (proposed/approved/rejected) and queue priority live in workflow.db (ticket_queue), recorded in its history, set through the library and ''workflow ticket approve|reject|priority'', so the database stays the only store.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 41, 'story', '1073', '- **M.TIX-US-G3 ⬜** As a Dev, Workflow Desktop''s Queue view lists every repo''s open tickets in priority order; I approve, reject (with a reason; it closes wont-do) and reorder them by drag and drop or by keyboard (buttons, Alt+Up/Down), each change announced to screen readers.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 42, 'story', '1074', '- **M.TIX-US-G4 ⬜** As a Dev, Workflow Desktop''s Tickets view lists every ticket in every repo, filterable by repo, status, type and approval, searchable by ID, summary and ref, sortable by column, with closed and wont-do tickets hidden until I show archived.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 43, 'story', '1075', '- **M.TIX-US-G5 ⬜** As a Dev, selecting a ticket opens a detail pane with its fields, history and links both ways (linked IDs focus that ticket, blocked state shown), where I close it, wont-do it, set its ref, correct its type with a reason and add or remove links.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 44, 'story', '1076', '- **M.TIX-US-G6 ⬜** As a Dev, Ctrl+N in Workflow Desktop files a new ticket (repo, type, summary, ref), remembering the last repo and type.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 45, 'story', '1077', '- **M.TIX-US-G7 ✅** As a Dev, Workflow Desktop shows agents'' ticket changes within seconds without a manual refresh, and a Sync button runs ''workflow db sync'' and shows its result.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 46, 'story', '1078', '- **M.TIX-US-G8 ⬜** As a Dev who relies on assistive tech, Workflow Desktop meets WCAG 2.2 AA: contrast, keyboard-only use, visible unobscured focus, names and roles, live regions, 200% zoom, high-contrast mode, 24px targets and a dragging alternative, proved by tests and an Accessibility Insights FastPass.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 47, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 48, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 49, 'epic', 'H', '## Epic H — Better than Jira');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 50, 'story', '1079', '- **M.TIX-US-H1 ⬜** As a Dev or Agent, I add append-only comments to a ticket (author, time, markdown), shown in its history, without rewording the ticket row.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 51, 'story', '1080', '- **M.TIX-US-H2 ⬜** As a Dev, a ticket has a markdown description separate from its one-line summary, and rewording the summary is a recorded correction with a reason, like CorrectType.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 52, 'story', '1081', '- **M.TIX-US-H3 ⬜** As a Dev, I tag tickets with labels and components and filter by them in the CLI and Workflow Desktop.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 53, 'story', '1082', '- **M.TIX-US-H4 ⬜** As a Dev, each ticket carries an effort estimate, seeded from the Orchestrator''s TicketCosts actuals for similar tickets and editable, so the queue can sort by smallest effort from the database.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 54, 'story', '1083', '- **M.TIX-US-H5 ⬜** As a Dev, I see which agent, CLI or worktree is working a ticket and since when, from the Orchestrator''s assignments, in the list and detail pane.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 55, 'story', '1084', '- **M.TIX-US-H6 ⬜** As a Dev, a Board view shows tickets in columns Proposed, Approved, In progress and Done, and moving a card (drag or keyboard) changes its approval or status.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 56, 'story', '1085', '- **M.TIX-US-H7 ⬜** As a Dev, I filter with a query language (repo:M.FLOW type:fix status:open label:ui ''text'') and save named filters for reuse in the CLI and Desktop.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 57, 'story', '1086', '- **M.TIX-US-H8 ⬜** As a Dev, I select many tickets and approve, reject, close, label or reprioritize them in one action.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 58, 'story', '1087', '- **M.TIX-US-H9 ⬜** As a Dev, Ctrl+Z undoes my last Workflow Desktop action by writing a compensating, recorded change, never by deleting history.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 59, 'story', '1088', '- **M.TIX-US-H10 ⬜** As a Dev, Ctrl+K opens a command palette to jump to any ticket or story by ID or text and run any command by name.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 60, 'story', '1089', '- **M.TIX-US-H11 ⬜** As a Dev, Workflow Desktop shows and edits a repo''s epics and stories (text, status, acceptance, evidence) and their implements links to tickets.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 61, 'story', '1090', '- **M.TIX-US-H12 ⬜** As a Dev, a dependency graph shows a ticket''s requires chain both ways, with what''s blocking it highlighted (and a text list for screen readers).');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 62, 'story', '1091', '- **M.TIX-US-H13 ⬜** As a Dev, an activity feed shows every ticket change across the workspace as it happens, and a toast tells me when an agent closes a ticket.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 63, 'story', '1092', '- **M.TIX-US-H14 ⬜** As a Dev, a ticket lists the commits whose subject names it, in every repo, with links to them on GitHub.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 64, 'story', '1093', '- **M.TIX-US-H15 ⬜** As a Dev, a metrics view shows throughput, cycle time (opened to closed), and open tickets by repo and type over time.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 65, 'story', '1094', '- **M.TIX-US-H16 ⬜** As a Dev, I export a filtered ticket list to CSV or markdown.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 66, 'story', '1095', '- **M.TIX-US-H17 ⬜** As a Dev, filing a ticket offers a template per type (fix: symptom, cause, test; feature: story, acceptance) and warns when a similar open ticket already exists.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 67, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 68, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 69, 'epic', 'I', '## Epic I — Storage: GitHub or local database');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 70, 'story', '1096', '- **M.TIX-US-I1 ⬜** As a Dev, once the GitHub Issues spike (M.TIX-T50) reports, I decide whether Issues becomes the ticket store or a mirror of workflow.db, and a two-way sync prototype runs behind the same library API so the CLI, hooks and orchestrator don''t change.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('MindAttic.Tickets', 71, 'raw', NULL, '');
