INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 1, 'epic', 'A', '## Epic A — Detection');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 2, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 3, 'story', '698', '- **OC-US-A1 🟡** As an operator, I can scan public GitHub for leaked credentials across many providers (LLM, cloud, VCS, payments, comms, DB URIs, private keys), so I find real exposures. *Given a GitHub PAT, When I run `opencreds --headless`, Then it searches each provider needle, fetches matches, and records `Finding` rows.* *(Shipped: `Scraper.RunAsync` + `Patterns.All` in [`v2/Cli/Scraper.cs`](../v2/Cli/Scraper.cs), [`v2/Shared/Patterns.cs`](../v2/Shared/Patterns.cs). No verifying test.)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 4, 'story', '699', '- **OC-US-A2 🟡** As a researcher, the scanner records metadata only and never retains the raw secret, so the project is IRB-defensible ([OC-LAW-1](BIBLE.md#OC-LAW-1)). *Given a match, When it is recorded, Then only SHA-256 + 16-char prefix + length persist.* *(Shipped: `Scraper.Fingerprint`, `rawKey = null!` after hashing. NO automated test asserts non-retention — this invariant is the #1 thing to test.)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 5, 'story', '700', '- **OC-US-A3 🟡** As an operator, I can opt into high-false-positive PlainTextPassword patterns separately, so they never pollute the default scan. *Given `--include-passwords`, When I scan, Then `Patterns.WithPasswords()` is used; otherwise it is not.* *(Shipped: `Patterns.WithPasswords`, gated by the `--include-passwords` flag in [`v2/Cli/Program.cs`](../v2/Cli/Program.cs).)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 6, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 7, 'epic', 'B', '## Epic B — Disclosure');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 8, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 9, 'story', '701', '- **OC-US-B1 ✅** As an operator, the scanner never auto-discloses until I flip a category on, so innocent repos aren''t harmed ([OC-LAW-2](BIBLE.md#OC-LAW-2)). *Given all exposure types default `auto_inform=false`, When the notify pass runs, Then it sends nothing.* *(Shipped: `Scraper.SendPendingNoticesAsync` auto-inform gate; seed defaults `AutoInform=false` in [`v2/Shared/Db.cs`](../v2/Shared/Db.cs). verified by `Notify_pass_sends_nothing_while_every_type_is_auto_inform_off`.)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 10, 'story', '702', '- **OC-US-B2 ✅** As an operator, I can file a courtesy issue on a leaker''s repo with the fingerprint (never the secret) when it has no private vulnerability reporting, so they can rotate. *Given a finding on a repo without private reporting, When I send a notice, Then a GitHub issue is opened and a `github_issue` Notice recorded.* *(Shipped: `NoticeService.SendAsync` → `GitHubClient.OpenIssueAsync`. verified by `Repo_without_private_reporting_falls_back_to_public_issue`; also `Notify_pass_falls_back_to_public_issue_when_private_reporting_is_off`.)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 11, 'story', '703', '- **OC-US-B3 ✅** As an operator, sending a notice twice for the same finding is a no-op on either channel, so I never spam a repo. *Given an existing `sent` notice, When I send again, Then it returns `Skipped=true` without calling GitHub.* *(Shipped: idempotency checks in `NoticeService.SendAsync` and `SendVulnerabilityReportAsync`. verified by `Sending_an_issue_twice_is_a_no_op`; also `Finding_already_disclosed_by_issue_is_skipped_without_any_GitHub_call`, `Finding_already_disclosed_by_advisory_is_skipped_without_any_GitHub_call`.)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 12, 'story', '704', '- **OC-US-B4 ✅** As an operator, disclosure goes through GitHub''s private vulnerability reporting when the repo has it enabled and falls back to a public issue otherwise, so security findings use the private channel first. *Given a repo with private vulnerability reporting, When a notice is sent from the CLI notify pass or the Findings page, Then a `github_advisory` Notice is recorded instead of a public issue; a transient advisory failure is recorded as failed and never goes public.* *(Shipped: `NoticeService.SendVulnerabilityReportAsync` in [`v2/Shared/NoticeService.cs`](../v2/Shared/NoticeService.cs), called by `Scraper.SendPendingNoticesAsync` and the Findings page Send/Retry button. verified by `Repo_with_private_reporting_gets_a_private_advisory_and_no_public_issue`; also `Transient_advisory_failure_never_goes_public`, `Rate_limited_403_is_a_transient_failure_not_unavailable`, `Notify_pass_discloses_through_private_advisory_first`, `Send_button_files_a_private_advisory_not_a_public_issue`.)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 13, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 14, 'epic', 'C', '## Epic C — Remediation tracking');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 15, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 16, 'story', '705', '- **OC-US-C1 🟡** As a researcher, each run re-checks existing findings to see if the leak was removed, so I can measure time-to-remediate. *Given prior findings, When the recheck pass runs, Then it re-fetches + re-hashes and writes a `RemediationCheck` (`present`/`removed`/`repo_gone`/`file_gone`).* *(Shipped: `Scraper.RecheckRemediationsAsync`.)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 17, 'story', '706', '- **OC-US-C2 🟡** As an operator, remediation rechecks are capped per run, so a large DB doesn''t burn the whole API budget. *Given `--max-rechecks N`, When the pass runs, Then at most N findings are re-checked, stalest first.* *(Shipped: `_maxRechecks` ordering by `CheckedAtUtc`.)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 18, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 19, 'epic', 'D', '## Epic D — Review UI (Blazor)');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 20, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 21, 'story', '707', '- **OC-US-D1 🟡** As a reviewer, I see a live, paginated table of every finding with notice + remediation status, so I can triage. *(Shipped: [`v2/Blazor/Components/Pages/Findings.razor`](../v2/Blazor/Components/Pages/Findings.razor), 3s live polling.)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 22, 'story', '708', '- **OC-US-D2 🟡** As a researcher, I see KPIs and charts (cumulative findings/notices/remediations, time-to-remediate, by-provider, status donut), so I can report aggregates. *(Shipped: [`v2/Blazor/Components/Pages/Visualizations.razor`](../v2/Blazor/Components/Pages/Visualizations.razor) + [`v2/Blazor/VizData.cs`](../v2/Blazor/VizData.cs).)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 23, 'story', '709', '- **OC-US-D3 🟡** As an operator, I can pause/resume the scanner and toggle per-type auto-inform from the UI, so I control disclosure without restarting the CLI. *(Shipped: [`v2/Blazor/Components/Pages/Settings.razor`](../v2/Blazor/Components/Pages/Settings.razor) writing `ScannerControl` + `SetAutoInform`.)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 24, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 25, 'epic', 'E', '## Epic E — Operations');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 26, 'raw', NULL, '');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 27, 'story', '710', '- **OC-US-E1 🟡** As an operator, the scanner loops forever and never crashes on a 403, so it can run unattended ([OC-LAW-3](BIBLE.md#OC-LAW-3)). *(Shipped: `RunLoopAsync` + `GitHubClient.HandleRateLimitAsync`.)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 28, 'story', '711', '- **OC-US-E2 🟡** As a CI user, `--headless` with no `--loop` runs a single pass and exits non-zero on failure, so it is automatable. *(Shipped: one-shot branch in [`v2/Cli/Program.cs`](../v2/Cli/Program.cs).)*');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('OpenCredentials', 29, 'story', '712', '- **OC-US-E3 🟡** As an operator, multiple scanners can run concurrently against one DB without double-scanning a file ([OC-LAW-5](BIBLE.md#OC-LAW-5)). *(Shipped: atomic `Db.ClaimScan`/`ReleaseScan` via PK uniqueness. Concurrency is asserted by structure, not by a test.)*');
