Mode `SuppressionFire` + HitsPerTarget `HitManyTimes`. Note: in the decompiled code SuppressionFire and MultipleTargetOverwatch behave the same; HitManyTimes is the difference. The enemy AI already counts overwatch areas as threats when pathing (AiBrainHelper reads PartOverwatch.OverwatchArea), so enemies should avoid the zone. Expensive: ends turn; consider a cooldown or ammo cost.', 'Suppression: aimed cone that pins enemies in place. **It fires only when a target moves**; shooting, casting or other actions inside the cone do not trigger it. A suppressed enemy may stay put and act freely, but every move it makes inside the cone draws a shot: the ranged equivalent of an Attack of Opportunity. Lasts until your next turn.

Engine facts (Code.dll, `OverwatchController`):
- Two trigger sources feed the same list: `HandleEntityPositionChanged` (any position update; `Entity.OnPositionChanged` raises it, likely many times per move) and `HandleUnitCommandDidAct` (any ability whose blueprint has `UsingInOverwatchArea: WillCauseAttack`). Then `Tick()` calls `PartOverwatch.TryTriggerAttack` for each overwatcher containing the unit.
- Mode only changes whether the part `Stop()`s after a shot (`Overwatch` stops; `SuppressionFire`/`MultipleTargetOverwatch` don''t). HitsPerTarget `HitOnce` skips units already shot.

So the rule can''t be done in data alone. Needs a small C# (Harmony) patch:
1. **Movement only:** for parts in `SuppressionFire` mode, ignore triggers that came from `HandleUnitCommandDidAct`, and act only on position changes.
2. **One shot per move (AoO-like):** throttle so a single move command draws one shot (or one per cell left inside the cone; decide in testing), not one per position update. Track the mover''s current move command and reset per command.
Blueprint side: Mode `SuppressionFire`, HitsPerTarget `HitManyTimes`, cone ~8 cells / 45–60°, ends the turn. The enemy AI already treats overwatch areas as threats when pathing (`AiBrainHelper` reads `PartOverwatch.OverwatchArea`), which matches "forces them to stay in place".
Ships as a UnityModManager mod or an Owlcat mod Scripts assembly, the same C# home as RTO-T12 (drag-to-size cone).

Acceptance: an enemy in the cone that shoots without moving takes no fire; one that moves takes a shot per move (not a burst of shots per step); stops at your next turn.');

`AbilityEffectOverwatch` Mode `Overwatch` (PartOverwatch.TryTriggerAttack calls Stop() after the first shot in this mode), HitsPerTarget `HitOnce`, `UseFirstWeaponAbility: true` (the weapon''s single shot). Zone: a `Circle` BlueprintAttackPattern around the unit (radius ~ weapon range; start 10 cells), no aiming. `WarhammerEndTurn` with `clearMPInsteadOfEndingTurn: false` (ends turn, like XCOM). Base it on the live, unused `Weapons/Abilities/Overwatch_BasicAbility` (1d271e94…, 2 AP) but with our own GUIDs and strings.
Triggers are engine rules: OverwatchController fires on enemy movement or on abilities with `UsingInOverwatchArea: WillCauseAttack`; overwatch ends at the unit''s next turn or when it acts.', '**Name: Reaction Overwatch** (renamed from Twitch Overwatch by the user, 2026-10-26). Display name, strings and file names use "Reaction Overwatch".

XCOM 2 overwatch: shoot the first enemy that moves or acts within range, once, then overwatch ends.

`AbilityEffectOverwatch` Mode `Overwatch` (PartOverwatch.TryTriggerAttack calls Stop() after the first shot in this mode), HitsPerTarget `HitOnce`, `UseFirstWeaponAbility: true` (the weapon''s single shot). Zone: a `Circle` BlueprintAttackPattern around the unit (radius ~ weapon range; start 10 cells), no aiming. `WarhammerEndTurn` with `clearMPInsteadOfEndingTurn: false` (ends turn, like XCOM). Base it on the live, unused `Weapons/Abilities/Overwatch_BasicAbility` (1d271e94…, 2 AP) but with our own GUIDs and strings.
Triggers are engine rules: OverwatchController fires on enemy movement or on abilities with `UsingInOverwatchArea: WillCauseAttack`; overwatch ends at the unit''s next turn or when it acts.');

Engine facts (Code.dll, `OverwatchController`):
- Two trigger sources feed the same list: `HandleEntityPositionChanged` (any position update; `Entity.OnPositionChanged` raises it, likely many times per move) and `HandleUnitCommandDidAct` (any ability whose blueprint has `UsingInOverwatchArea: WillCauseAttack`). Then `Tick()` calls `PartOverwatch.TryTriggerAttack` for each overwatcher containing the unit.
- Mode only changes whether the part `Stop()`s after a shot (`Overwatch` stops; `SuppressionFire`/`MultipleTargetOverwatch` don''t). HitsPerTarget `HitOnce` skips units already shot.

So the rule can''t be done in data alone. Needs a small C# (Harmony) patch:
1. **Movement only:** for parts in `SuppressionFire` mode, ignore triggers that came from `HandleUnitCommandDidAct`, and act only on position changes.
2. **One shot per move (AoO-like):** throttle so a single move command draws one shot (or one per cell left inside the cone; decide in testing), not one per position update. Track the mover''s current move command and reset per command.
Blueprint side: Mode `SuppressionFire`, HitsPerTarget `HitManyTimes`, cone ~8 cells / 45–60°, ends the turn. The enemy AI already treats overwatch areas as threats when pathing (`AiBrainHelper` reads `PartOverwatch.OverwatchArea`), which matches "forces them to stay in place".
Ships as a UnityModManager mod or an Owlcat mod Scripts assembly, the same C# home as RTO-T12 (drag-to-size cone).

Acceptance: an enemy in the cone that shoots without moving takes no fire; one that moves takes a shot per move (not a burst of shots per step); stops at your next turn.', '**Suppression is single-target** (user, 2026-10-26): you target one enemy. While suppressed it can stay put and act freely, but if it moves, you take a ranged attack of opportunity at it. That keeps it pinned in place. Lasts until your next turn. Only movement triggers it; its attacks and abilities don''t. Other enemies moving nearby are ignored.

Engine facts (Code.dll, `OverwatchController`):
- `PartOverwatch` is zone-based: it fires at any enemy whose cells are in `OverwatchArea`. Triggers come from `HandleEntityPositionChanged` (every position update, likely many per move) and `HandleUnitCommandDidAct` (abilities with `UsingInOverwatchArea: WillCauseAttack`).
- Mode only controls whether the part `Stop()`s after a shot; `HitManyTimes` lets the same unit be shot again.

