## Rules
- Press the button, then move the cursor: the cone resizes live. A farther cursor gives a longer, narrower cone; a closer one gives a shorter, wider cone, capped at weapon range. Click to lock it in.
- **Shots = the AP you had left when you cast it.** Casting spends all remaining AP and ends your turn. You need at least 1 AP to cast.
- Every enemy that moves or acts inside the cone draws a shot until the shots run out or your next turn starts.
- Each shot is the weapon''s normal single shot. Accuracy falls with distance through the game''s own distance factor; optionally add a further penalty for wide cones.
- **Re-shooting the same enemy** (user, 2026-10-26): allowed, but only after it has moved at least **2 tiles** since you last shot it, so it doesn''t take a full attack every square. Keep the 2-tile minimum as a tunable constant.
- **Spread fire first:** cycling between enemies always takes priority. While any enemy in the cone hasn''t been shot yet, an already-shot enemy moving again draws no fire; the shot is held for the others. Only when there''s no choice (every enemy in the cone has been shot, or it''s the only one) does it fire at the same enemy again, still subject to the 2-tile rule.
- Open question for testing: does a re-shot need movement, or can an already-shot enemy acting (shooting or casting) in the cone also draw a second shot? Proposal: only movement re-triggers; actions can only draw a first shot.

## Engine pieces (Code.dll)
- Zone: `AbilityEffectOverwatch` → `PartOverwatch`, Mode `MultipleTargetOverwatch` (doesn''t Stop after a shot), with HitsPerTarget set by the open question. Triggers come from `OverwatchController` (position changes, and abilities with `UsingInOverwatchArea: WillCauseAttack`).
- Drag cone: every pattern ability''s shape comes from `AbilityAoEPatternSettings.GetOrientedPattern(ability, casterNode, targetNode)`. The targeting preview (`AbilityPatternRange`) calls it as the cursor moves, and `AbilityEffectOverwatch.GetOverwatchArea` calls it when the zone is set, so preview and zone match. Harmony-patch it for this ability only to return `AoEPattern.Cone(angle(d), radius(d))` from the caster→cursor distance (`AoEPattern.Cone`/`CopyAndOverrideRadius`/`GridPatterns.ConstructPattern` build any size at runtime).
- Re-shot and priority rules: `PartOverwatch.TryTriggerAttack` only knows HitOnce (never again) or HitManyTimes (every trigger), so these need C#. Per overwatcher, keep each enemy''s cell at its last shot and its shot count. On a trigger, (1) skip if it was shot and has moved < 2 cells (grid distance) since; (2) skip if it was shot and any enemy currently inside the cone hasn''t been shot yet; otherwise fire and record. Position triggers arrive many times per move (`Entity.OnPositionChanged`), so the distance check also rate-limits them.
- Shot budget: no data component spends "all remaining AP", so in C#: on cast, read the caster''s remaining AP into the overwatch part (or a stacking buff via `AbilityEffectOverwatch.ApplyingBuffs`, whose rank shows the shots left), decrement on each `UnitOverwatchAttack`, then `Stop()` at 0. End the turn with `WarhammerEndTurn` (`clearMPInsteadOfEndingTurn: false`). Candidate to inspect: `WarhammerAbilityCostChangeContextValue`.
- Accuracy: `RuleCalculateHitChances.OnTriggerRanged` multiplies by `RuleCalculateAbilityDistanceFactor`. Extra overwatch penalty: a buff via `ApplyingBuffs` if a hit-chance modifier component exists, else a small patch on that rule for overwatch shots.
- C# home: the same assembly as Suppression''s movement-only rule (RTO-T8), either a UnityModManager mod (the user runs UMM: Brevity, ToyBox) or an Owlcat mod Scripts assembly.

